# ----------------------------- the engine's files are at fixed paths, whatever XDG says (ADR-0021) ----
# XDG_CONFIG_HOME is often set only in an interactive shell. kb-schedule install then wrote
# schedule.conf under it, and the cron or systemd run, without it, read ~/.config: preparation off and
# no saved PATH, silently. Install under XDG_*, run without it: the conf is still found. And no XDG_*
# variable moves the packets, the reports or the log.
